{"dossier":"D06","entry_points":[{"sids":["mm/gup_test.c::gup_test_data"],"text":"Debug node open allocates session and mutex; release stops pin and frees. Ioctl splits benchmark/dump vs longterm start/stop/read. Benchmark validates range, loops chunkwise under killable lock, times pin and release, verifies and dumps. Longterm needs aligned range, no active pin, optional write/fast."},{"sids":["mm/hmm.c::hmm_walk_ops","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_walk_test","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_walk_pmd","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_walk_pud.alt_1","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_walk_pud.alt_2","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_walk_hugetlb_entry.alt_1","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_walk_hugetlb_entry.alt_2","mm/pagewalk.c::walk_page_test","mm/pagewalk.c::__walk_page_range"],"text":"HMM dispatch binds middle/hole/huge handlers with eligibility test; upper/huge exist in one build only. Walk test routes PFNMAP to hole/skip; range entry rejects hugetlb installs, runs pre/post hooks."}],"exports":[{"sids":["mm/highmem.c::kmap_high","mm/highmem.c::kmap_high_get","mm/highmem.c::kunmap_high","mm/highmem.c::page_address","mm/highmem.c::set_page_address","mm/highmem.c::__kmap_to_page","mm/highmem.c::__kmap_flush_unused","mm/highmem.c::__nr_free_highpages","mm/highmem.c::__totalhigh_pages","mm/highmem.c::zero_user_segments","mm/highmem.c::page_address_init"],"text":"High-memory maps with refcounts, lookup, unmap, page/address translation, reverse lookup, flush, boot init, free/total counts, and multi-range zeroing via temp maps."},{"sids":["mm/highmem.c::__kmap_local_page_prot","mm/highmem.c::__kmap_local_pfn_prot","mm/highmem.c::kunmap_local_indexed","mm/highmem.c::kmap_get_pte","mm/highmem.c::__kmap_pte","mm/highmem.c::__kmap_local_sched_out","mm/highmem.c::__kmap_local_sched_in","mm/highmem.c::kmap_local_fork"],"text":"Thread-local temp maps by page/frame with caller protection, indexed unmap, direct low-memory return, fixed-slot install, scheduler save/restore, and fork empty check."},{"sids":["mm/pagewalk.c::walk_page_range","mm/pagewalk.c::walk_page_range_mm_unsafe","mm/hmm.c::hmm_range_fault","mm/hmm.c::hmm_dma_map_alloc","mm/hmm.c::hmm_dma_map_free","mm/huge_memory.c::huge_zero_init.alt_1","mm/huge_memory.c::huge_zero_shrinker_exit.alt_1","mm/huge_memory.c::mm_put_huge_zero_folio.alt_1","mm/huge_memory.c::__read_mostly.alt_2"],"text":"Range walks with callback checks, sync HMM fault wrapper, DMA map alloc/free with reserved-space handling, and one-shot huge-zero folio boot setup."}],"extracts":["36069648a6d08111f3cbb7721b68fc981a07e4915cab1dd336db86fe9148dd10","8e743c6d6ea18b9d9f257e67ff3e0359851a790662e8f612e3b399e2a9b9acc5","f6ae01771db5fa650536956c0f1f32a618095a5e3fee04f054efc0bf8ef116d8"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["mm/gup_test.c::gup_test_data"],"text":"Overflow, misalignment, unknown commands, empty or oversized ranges, bad flags, second session, copy faults, and interrupted locks fail; unbalanced nesting or bad counts warn or trap."},{"sids":["mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_walk_pmd","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_handle_pte","mm/hmm.c::hmm_dma_map_pfn"],"text":"Middle reads run lockless with recheck, relying on invalidation; faulting over special entries hard-fails; peer/link/sync/phys failures return mapping-error sentinel."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["mm/highmem.c::flush_all_zero_pkmaps","mm/highmem.c::get_pkmap_color.alt_1","mm/highmem.c::get_pkmap_color.alt_2","mm/highmem.c::get_next_pkmap_nr","mm/highmem.c::no_more_pkmaps","mm/highmem.c::get_pkmap_entries_count","mm/highmem.c::get_pkmap_wait_queue_head"],"text":"Count zero free, one flushable, higher active; global flush clears ones with single range flush. Color zero, round-robin scan masked, wrap at zero, full window, single wait queue."},{"sids":["mm/highmem.c::kmap_local_calc_idx","mm/highmem.c::arch_kmap_local_map_idx","mm/highmem.c::arch_kmap_local_unmap_idx","mm/highmem.c::kmap_local_idx_push","mm/highmem.c::kmap_local_idx","mm/highmem.c::kmap_local_idx_pop","mm/highmem.c::arch_kmap_local_post_map","mm/highmem.c::arch_kmap_local_pre_unmap","mm/highmem.c::arch_kmap_local_post_unmap","mm/highmem.c::arch_kmap_local_set_pte","mm/highmem.c::arch_kmap_local_high_get","mm/highmem.c::kmap_high_unmap_local"],"text":"Nesting steps within max with per-CPU slots. Map disables migration/preemption, requires empty slot, installs; unmap validates and clears. Default hooks no-op."},{"sids":["mm/hmm.c::hmm_pte_need_fault","mm/hmm.c::hmm_range_need_fault","mm/hmm.c::hmm_pfns_fill","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_handle_pmd","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_handle_pte","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_walk_hole","mm/hmm.c::pmd_to_hmm_pfn_flags","mm/hmm.c::pte_to_hmm_pfn_flags","mm/hmm.c::pud_to_hmm_pfn_flags","mm/hmm.c::hmm_pfn_flags_order","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_handle_absent_pmd.alt_1","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_handle_absent_pmd.alt_2","mm/hmm.c::hmm_dma_unmap_pfn"],"text":"Fault need blends entry/range bits; fills keep mapping attrs. Absent gives none else valid/writable plus order. Holes fail when faulting else error/empty. Own private direct, foreign faults, migration waits. Bad areas skip. Huge expands per-page. Unmap needs valid+mapped."},{"sids":["mm/pagewalk.c::hugetlb_entry_end","mm/pagewalk.c::walk_hugetlb_range.alt_2","mm/huge_memory.c::__read_mostly.alt_1","mm/huge_memory.c::file_thp_enabled","mm/huge_memory.c::vma_file_bypass_thp_tuneables","mm/huge_memory.c::vma_file_allow_thp_tuneables","mm/huge_memory.c::vma_file_check_thp_tuneables","mm/huge_memory.c::vma_can_map_huge_file","mm/huge_memory.c::__thp_vma_allowable_orders","mm/shmem.c::shmem_allowable_huge_orders","mm/shmem.c::shmem_get_orders_within_size","mm/shmem.c::shmem_huge_global_enabled.alt_1","mm/shmem.c::shmem_huge_global_enabled.alt_2","mm/shmem.c::vma_is_anon_shmem","mm/shmem.c::SHMEM_SB","mm/huge_memory.c::pr_fmt","mm/huge_memory.c::CREATE_TRACE_POINTS","mm/huge_memory.c::split_underused_thp","mm/huge_memory.c::__read_mostly.alt_4","mm/huge_memory.c::__read_mostly.alt_5","mm/huge_memory.c::__read_mostly.alt_6","mm/huge_memory.c::__initdata"],"text":"Hugetlb clamps to one page; one build no-ops. THP defaults defrag plus zero; file needs regular folio support. Tunables honor force/always/advised. Orders intersect support, prune by fit, shmem unions sets with deny/force. Anon by ops; split default; policy globals."}],"locks":[{"sids":["mm/highmem.c::lock_kmap.alt_1","mm/highmem.c::unlock_kmap.alt_1","mm/highmem.c::lock_kmap_any.alt_1","mm/highmem.c::unlock_kmap_any.alt_1","mm/highmem.c::lock_kmap.alt_2","mm/highmem.c::unlock_kmap.alt_2","mm/highmem.c::lock_kmap_any.alt_2","mm/highmem.c::unlock_kmap_any.alt_2"],"text":"One build disables interrupts, another plain; atomic callers use flag-saving variants. Lock spans lookup, alloc, bump, flush, unmap, released across sleeps."},{"sids":["mm/pagewalk.c::process_mm_walk_lock","mm/pagewalk.c::process_vma_walk_lock","mm/mmu_notifier.c::mmu_interval_read_begin","mm/huge_memory.c::deferred_split_key","mm/huge_memory.c::deferred_split_lru","mm/huge_memory.c::deferred_split_shrinker","mm/huge_memory.c::huge_zero_refcount","mm/huge_memory.c::huge_zero_lock","mm/huge_memory.c::huge_zero_folio_shrinker"],"text":"Walk asserts mmap read/write or per-VMA ownership. Interval samples generation, sleeps inside invalidation, leaves retry to caller. Deferred split has LRU/shrinker; zero folio has spinlock, refcount, shrinker."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F1"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F3"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["mm/hmm.c::hmm_range_fault_unlocked_timeout","mm/hmm.c::hmm_range_fault_locked","mm/hmm.c::hmm_do_fault","mm/hmm.c::hmm_record_fault"],"text":"Range fault repeats walk then external fault; busy/invalidation restarts from progress, lock loss becomes busy unless fatal signal. Unlocked variant enforces deadline, tracks lock, retries only busy."},{"sids":["mm/highmem.c::map_new_virtual","mm/pagewalk.c::walk_hugetlb_range.alt_1"],"text":"Alloc scans for zero slot, flushes on wrap, sleeps on shared wait then rechecks, installs and marks single ref. Hugetlb holds read lock, delivers present to callback, missing to hole, stops on error."},{"sids":["mm/hmm.c::hmm_dma_map_pfn"],"text":"Mapped pages return existing address; else classify peer, fail unknown, link plus sync reserved space with unlink on failure, or map physical directly, marking success."}],"structs":[{"sids":["mm/gup_test.h::gup_test","mm/gup_test.h::GUP_TEST_MAX_PAGES_TO_DUMP","mm/gup_test.h::pin_longterm_test","mm/gup_test.h::PIN_LONGTERM_TEST_FLAG_USE_WRITE","mm/gup_test.h::PIN_LONGTERM_TEST_FLAG_USE_FAST","mm/hmm.c::hmm_vma_walk"],"text":"Test descriptor holds durations, address/len, page limit, flags, and 8-slot dump selection; longterm adds write/fast flags; HMM cursor holds range, lock-loss flag, progress, fault need."},{"sids":["mm/highmem.c::pkmap_count","mm/highmem.c::kmap_lock","mm/highmem.c::pkmap_page_table","mm/highmem.c::page_address_map","mm/highmem.c::page_address_maps","mm/highmem.c::page_address_slot","mm/highmem.c::page_address_htable","mm/highmem.c::PA_HASH_ORDER","mm/highmem.c::page_slot"],"text":"Persistent state has slot count array, aligned central lock, window table, page-address records in hashed bucket lists with per-bucket locks, order seven, slot lookup by page."},{"sids":["mm/gup_test.h::GUP_FAST_BENCHMARK","mm/gup_test.h::PIN_FAST_BENCHMARK","mm/gup_test.h::PIN_LONGTERM_BENCHMARK","mm/gup_test.h::GUP_BASIC_TEST","mm/gup_test.h::PIN_BASIC_TEST","mm/gup_test.h::DUMP_USER_PAGES_TEST","mm/gup_test.h::PIN_LONGTERM_TEST_START","mm/gup_test.h::PIN_LONGTERM_TEST_STOP","mm/gup_test.h::PIN_LONGTERM_TEST_READ","mm/gup_test.h::GUP_TEST_FLAG_DUMP_PAGES_USE_PIN","mm/highmem.c::KM_INCR.alt_1","mm/highmem.c::KM_INCR.alt_2","mm/hmm.c::HMM_FAULT_PENDING","mm/hmm.c::HMM_FAULT_UNLOCKED","mm/hmm.c::anon_1","mm/hmm.c::anon_2","mm/huge_memory.c::HUGE_ZERO_UNSET_PFN","mm/huge_memory.c::__read_mostly.alt_3"],"text":"Benchmark/dump ioctls share magic g numbers 1-6; longterm start/stop/read use 7-9 with write/none/write. Dump table 8, pin flag 1, write 1, fast 2, step 1 or 2. HMM pending EAGAIN, unlocked ENOLCK, fault bits 0/1; huge-zero unset all-ones."}],"stubs":[{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::BUG_ON.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::BUG_ON.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_3","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::BUG.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::BUG.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON.alt_1","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON.alt_2","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON.alt_3","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/fixmap.h::__fix_to_virt","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/kconfig.h::IS_ENABLED","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/hugetlb.h::huge_ptep_get","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/array_size.h::ARRAY_SIZE","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/fortify-string.h::memset","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/uapi/linux/stat.h::S_ISREG","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/asm-generic/cacheflush.h::flush_dcache_page","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"include/linux/uaccess.h::copy_from_user","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D17"},{"sid":"i